    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/events-api--test-event-deliver",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Exercises the value-manipulation event system calls without any waking or blocking, validating both the resulting set of posted events and the previous value each call returns. Runs as a user-mode test so the event system calls are also exercised from an unprivileged thread.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize an event object and confirm it holds no events.\n- Post events and verify k_event_post() returns the prior set and ORs in the new bits.\n- Overwrite events with k_event_set() and verify it returns the prior set.\n- Use k_event_set_masked() to selectively set/clear bits and verify only the masked bits change while the returned value reports their prior state.\nExpected result:\n- After each call the stored events (read via k_event_test()) match the expected value, and each call returns the previous state of the affected bits.\nSee also: k_event_post()\nSee also: k_event_set()\nSee also: k_event_set_masked()\nSee also: k_event_test()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "events_api__test_event_deliver"
        }
      ],
      "name": "events_api__test_event_deliver",
      "summary": "Verify event posting and clearing primitives update stored events."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/events-api--test-event-receive",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Drives a receiver thread and two extra waiter threads through a scripted sequence of synchronization points to validate the blocking event APIs end to end: matching all-vs-any conditions, returning only the matching bits, optionally resetting the event before waiting, and waking multiple threads blocked on a single event object at once.\nTest steps:\n- Pre-load the event object and start a receiver thread plus two extra threads waiting with k_event_wait()/k_event_wait_all().\n- Walk the receiver through waits that should miss, partially match and fully match the posted events, checking the returned bits each time.\n- Repeat with the reset flag set and confirm the event is cleared before the new bits are posted.\n- Wake both extra threads via k_event_set() and collect the events they report back.\nExpected result:\n- Each wait returns exactly the matching bits (0 when the condition is not satisfied), reset-on-wait clears prior events, and all woken threads report the expected events.\nSee also: k_event_post()\nSee also: k_event_set()\nSee also: k_event_wait()\nSee also: k_event_wait_all()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "events_api__test_event_receive"
        }
      ],
      "name": "events_api__test_event_receive",
      "summary": "Verify multi-threaded waiting, reset-on-wait and waking of waiters."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/events-api--test-k-event-clear",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "k_event_clear() must reset exactly the requested events tracked by the event object, leave all other events untouched, report the prior state of the requested events, and be a no-op for events that are not currently set. Runs as a user-mode test so the clear system call is also exercised through its user-mode verifier.\nTest steps:\n- Verify the statically defined event object starts empty, then set a known pattern (0x33).\n- Clear a subset (0x11); verify the prior state of those events is returned and only the requested events are cleared (0x22 remains).\n- Clear the same subset again; verify it returns 0 (the events were no longer set) and nothing changes.\n- Clear all events; verify the event object ends up empty.\nExpected result:\n- Only the requested events are cleared, each call reports the prior state of the requested events, and clearing unset events changes nothing.\nSee also: k_event_clear()\nSee also: k_event_test()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "events_api__test_k_event_clear"
        }
      ],
      "name": "events_api__test_k_event_clear",
      "summary": "Verify k_event_clear() clears specified events."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/events-api--test-k-event-init",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "White-box test confirming that a freshly initialized event starts with no pending events and no threads parked on its wait queue, which is the precondition every other event operation relies on.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a k_event object with k_event_init().\n- Read the head of the event wait queue.\n- Read the event's set of posted events.\nExpected result:\n- The wait queue head is NULL (no waiters).\n- The set of posted events is 0.\nSee also: k_event_init()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "events_api__test_k_event_init"
        }
      ],
      "name": "events_api__test_k_event_init",
      "summary": "Verify that k_event_init() produces an empty, unowned event object."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/events-api--test-k-event-wait-all-safe",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The all-match \"safe\" wait variant returns and clears the requested bits only when every requested bit is present; a partial match returns nothing and leaves the object untouched. This test exercises both the no-match and the complete-match cases. Runs as a user-mode test.\nTest steps:\n- Set a known set of events on the object.\n- Wait-all for a set that is not fully present and verify 0 is returned.\n- Wait-all for a fully-present subset and verify exactly that subset is returned and consumed.\n- Repeat for the remaining bits.\nExpected result:\n- A partial match returns 0 and consumes nothing; a complete match returns the requested bits and removes them from the object.\nSee also: k_event_wait_all_safe()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "events_api__test_k_event_wait_all_safe"
        }
      ],
      "name": "events_api__test_k_event_wait_all_safe",
      "summary": "Verify k_event_wait_all_safe() consumes bits only on a full match."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/events-api--test-k-event-wait-safe",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The \"safe\" wait variant atomically clears the events it reports so a caller never observes the same event twice. This test confirms that requested bits present in the object are returned and removed, and that a subsequent wait for the same bits returns nothing. Runs as a user-mode test.\nTest steps:\n- Set a known set of events on the object.\n- Wait (any-match) for a subset and verify exactly that subset is returned.\n- Wait again for the same subset and verify no events are returned (the bits were consumed).\n- Repeat for the remaining bits, including an all-ones request.\nExpected result:\n- Each call returns only the matching bits that were present and removes them, so re-waiting for already-consumed bits yields 0.\nSee also: k_event_wait_safe()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "events_api__test_k_event_wait_safe"
        }
      ],
      "name": "events_api__test_k_event_wait_safe",
      "summary": "Verify k_event_wait_safe() consumes only the bits it returns."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fatal-exception--test-cpu-exception",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "An alternate thread executes an illegal instruction (architecture specific), which raises a CPU exception. The kernel's default exception handler reports K_ERR_CPU_EXCEPTION to the installed fatal error handler, which validates the reason code, and the offending thread is terminated while the test thread resumes.\nTest steps:\n- Create a cooperative thread whose entry point triggers a CPU exception.\n- Let the default exception handler run and deliver the reason code.\nExpected result:\n- The handler is invoked with K_ERR_CPU_EXCEPTION and the offending thread is terminated (rv is not TC_FAIL).\nSee also: k_sys_fatal_error_handler()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fatal_exception__test_cpu_exception"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fatal_exception__test_cpu_exception",
      "summary": "Verify a CPU exception in a thread is caught by the default handler."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fatal-exception--test-cpu-exception-extended",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Same contract as test_cpu_exception() but using a second architecture specific trigger (e.g. divide-by-zero on x86/MIPS, a distinct illegal instruction elsewhere). This widens coverage of the default exception path across the trigger mechanisms a given architecture provides.\nTest steps:\n- Create a cooperative thread whose entry point triggers a CPU exception via the alternate mechanism.\nExpected result:\n- The handler is invoked with K_ERR_CPU_EXCEPTION and the offending thread is terminated (rv is not TC_FAIL).\nSee also: k_sys_fatal_error_handler()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fatal_exception__test_cpu_exception_extended"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fatal_exception__test_cpu_exception_extended",
      "summary": "Verify an alternate CPU exception trigger is caught by the handler."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fatal-exception--test-except-reason-negative",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Companion to test_except_reason_positive() using a negative reason (-2) to confirm the reason code is delivered verbatim regardless of sign and is handled by the default fatal path.\nTest steps:\n- Create a thread that calls z_except_reason() with a negative reason.\n- Abort/join the thread and confirm it crashed as expected.\nExpected result:\n- The handler is invoked with the exact reason code supplied and the offending thread is terminated (rv is not TC_FAIL).\nSee also: k_sys_fatal_error_handler()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fatal_exception__test_except_reason_negative"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fatal_exception__test_except_reason_negative",
      "summary": "Verify an arbitrary negative reason code is propagated to the handler."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fatal-exception--test-except-reason-positive",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "An alternate thread raises a fatal error with an application-defined reason (INT_MAX) via z_except_reason(). A reason code that has no dedicated handler must still reach the default fatal handler unchanged, confirming the reason code identifies the error to the handler.\nTest steps:\n- Create a thread that calls z_except_reason() with a positive reason.\n- Abort/join the thread and confirm it crashed as expected.\nExpected result:\n- The handler is invoked with the exact reason code supplied and the offending thread is terminated (rv is not TC_FAIL).\nSee also: k_sys_fatal_error_handler()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fatal_exception__test_except_reason_positive"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fatal_exception__test_except_reason_positive",
      "summary": "Verify an arbitrary positive reason code is propagated to the handler."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fatal-exception--test-oops",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "An alternate thread calls k_oops(). This is the mechanism for code to flag a fatal error in the current context. The fatal handler receives K_ERR_KERNEL_OOPS and the offending thread is terminated, demonstrating both the trigger mechanism and that the application-supplied handler is consulted.\nTest steps:\n- Create a thread whose entry point calls k_oops().\n- Abort/join the thread and confirm it crashed as expected.\nExpected result:\n- The handler is invoked with K_ERR_KERNEL_OOPS and the offending thread is terminated (rv is not TC_FAIL).\nSee also: k_oops()\nSee also: k_sys_fatal_error_handler()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fatal_exception__test_oops"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fatal_exception__test_oops",
      "summary": "Verify k_oops() triggers a fatal error terminating the current thread."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fatal-exception--test-panic",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "An alternate thread calls k_panic(), the mechanism for code to signal an unrecoverable system error. The fatal handler receives K_ERR_KERNEL_PANIC. Because the test installs its own handler that returns, the offending thread is terminated and the test resumes.\nTest steps:\n- Create a thread whose entry point calls k_panic().\n- Abort/join the thread and confirm it crashed as expected.\nExpected result:\n- The handler is invoked with K_ERR_KERNEL_PANIC and the offending thread is terminated (rv is not TC_FAIL).\nSee also: k_panic()\nSee also: k_sys_fatal_error_handler()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fatal_exception__test_panic"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fatal_exception__test_panic",
      "summary": "Verify k_panic() triggers a fatal system error."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api--test-fifo-alloc-put",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Use k_fifo_alloc_put() to enqueue a data item that does not reserve space for the bookkeeping word, so the kernel allocates the container from the calling thread's resource pool. Verify the call succeeds and that the same data pointer is returned by a subsequent get.\nSee also: k_fifo_alloc_put()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api__test_fifo_alloc_put"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api__test_fifo_alloc_put",
      "summary": "Test enqueuing a data item to a FIFO with implicit memory allocation."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api--test-fifo-get-fail",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "When no data is queued, k_fifo_get() must return NULL rather than block indefinitely or return stale data. The contract is checked both with K_NO_WAIT (immediate) and with a finite timeout that is allowed to expire.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize an empty FIFO.\n- Call k_fifo_get() with K_NO_WAIT and verify it returns NULL.\n- Call k_fifo_get() with a finite timeout and verify it returns NULL.\nExpected result:\n- Both k_fifo_get() calls return NULL.\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api__test_fifo_get_fail"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api__test_fifo_get_fail",
      "summary": "Verify k_fifo_get() on an empty FIFO returns NULL."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api--test-fifo-is-empty-isr",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Same emptiness contract as the thread-context case, but the put/get/is_empty sequence is executed from interrupt context via irq_offload() to confirm k_fifo_is_empty() is ISR-safe.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a FIFO and assert it is empty from thread context.\n- From an ISR, put items (not empty) then get them all (empty again).\nExpected result:\n- k_fifo_is_empty() reports the correct state when called from an ISR.\nSee also: k_fifo_is_empty()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api__test_fifo_is_empty_isr"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api__test_fifo_is_empty_isr",
      "summary": "Verify k_fifo_is_empty() tracks FIFO contents in ISR context."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api--test-fifo-is-empty-thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "k_fifo_is_empty() must report true for a freshly initialized FIFO, false once items are enqueued, and true again after they are all dequeued. All operations run in thread context.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a FIFO and assert it is empty.\n- Put items and assert it is not empty.\n- Get all items and assert it is empty again.\nExpected result:\n- k_fifo_is_empty() reflects the presence or absence of queued data.\nSee also: k_fifo_is_empty()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api__test_fifo_is_empty_thread"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api__test_fifo_is_empty_thread",
      "summary": "Verify k_fifo_is_empty() tracks FIFO contents in thread context."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api--test-fifo-isr2thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Items are enqueued in thread context and dequeued from interrupt context (via irq_offload()), confirming k_fifo_get() is ISR-safe and the ISR receives every item in FIFO order. Run against both an init()ed and a DEFINE()d FIFO.\nTest steps:\n- In thread context, put items into the FIFO.\n- From an ISR, get all items, verify their order, and assert the FIFO is empty.\n- Repeat for a statically defined FIFO.\nExpected result:\n- The ISR dequeues every thread-enqueued item in order.\nSee also: k_fifo_put()\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api__test_fifo_isr2thread"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api__test_fifo_isr2thread",
      "summary": "Verify FIFO data passing from a thread to an ISR."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api--test-fifo-peek",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Enqueue two data items, then use k_fifo_peek_head() and k_fifo_peek_tail() to inspect the items at the front and back of the FIFO and verify the returned pointers match the first and last enqueued items without removing them (a subsequent get still returns both items in order). Peeking an empty FIFO returns NULL.\nSee also: k_fifo_peek_head(), k_fifo_peek_tail()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api__test_fifo_peek"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api__test_fifo_peek",
      "summary": "Test peeking at the front and back items of a FIFO."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api--test-fifo-thread2isr",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Items are enqueued from interrupt context (via irq_offload()) and dequeued in thread context, confirming k_fifo_put() is ISR-safe and the thread receives every item in FIFO order. Run against both an init()ed and a DEFINE()d FIFO.\nTest steps:\n- From an ISR, put items into the FIFO and assert it is not empty.\n- In thread context, get all items and verify their order.\n- Repeat for a statically defined FIFO.\nExpected result:\n- The thread dequeues every ISR-enqueued item in order.\nSee also: k_fifo_put()\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api__test_fifo_thread2isr"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api__test_fifo_thread2isr",
      "summary": "Verify FIFO data passing from an ISR to a thread."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api-1cpu--test-fifo-cancel-wait",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A thread blocked in k_fifo_get() with a long timeout must return immediately with NULL when another thread calls k_fifo_cancel_wait() on that FIFO, rather than waiting for its own timeout to expire. The test confirms both the NULL return and that it happened well before the 500 ms get timeout.\nTest steps:\n- Start a helper thread that sleeps briefly then calls k_fifo_cancel_wait().\n- In the main thread, call k_fifo_get() with a 500 ms timeout and time it.\n- Verify the get returned NULL and far sooner than its timeout.\n- Repeat for a statically defined FIFO.\nExpected result:\n- k_fifo_get() returns NULL promptly due to the cancel, not the timeout.\nSee also: k_fifo_cancel_wait()\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api_1cpu__test_fifo_cancel_wait"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api_1cpu__test_fifo_cancel_wait",
      "summary": "Verify k_fifo_cancel_wait() wakes a pending getter with NULL."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api-1cpu--test-fifo-loop",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Stresses the FIFO by cycling data through main-thread, ISR and spawned-thread contexts many times. Across every iteration the items must be passed without loss, duplication or reordering, exercising put/get stability when producers and consumers alternate between thread and interrupt context.\nTest steps:\n- For LOOPS iterations: put from the main thread, get then put from an ISR, and get from a spawned thread.\n- Verify each get returns the expected item.\nExpected result:\n- Data passes correctly and in order across all contexts on every iteration.\nSee also: k_fifo_put()\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api_1cpu__test_fifo_loop"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api_1cpu__test_fifo_loop",
      "summary": "Verify FIFO data integrity under repeated cross-context traffic."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-api-1cpu--test-fifo-thread2thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A consumer thread blocks on k_fifo_get() while the main thread enqueues items via the single, list and slist put APIs. The consumer must receive every item in FIFO order. The scenario is run against both a k_fifo_init()ed and a K_FIFO_DEFINE()d FIFO to confirm both initialization paths behave the same.\nTest steps:\n- Create a preemptible consumer thread that drains the FIFO.\n- From the main thread, put items using k_fifo_put(), k_fifo_put_list() and k_fifo_put_slist().\n- Synchronize on a semaphore once the consumer has read all items.\n- Repeat for a statically defined FIFO.\nExpected result:\n- The consumer dequeues every item in the order it was enqueued.\nSee also: k_fifo_put()\nSee also: k_fifo_put_list()\nSee also: k_fifo_put_slist()\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_api_1cpu__test_fifo_thread2thread"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_api_1cpu__test_fifo_thread2thread",
      "summary": "Verify FIFO data passing between two threads."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-timeout--test-timeout-non-empty-fifo",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "When data is already queued, k_fifo_get() must return it immediately regardless of the timeout argument. The contract is checked with both K_NO_WAIT and K_FOREVER, neither of which should block when data is present.\nTest steps:\n- Put an item, then k_fifo_get() with K_NO_WAIT and verify a non-NULL return.\n- Put an item, then k_fifo_get() with K_FOREVER and verify a non-NULL return.\nExpected result:\n- Both gets return the queued item without blocking.\nSee also: k_fifo_get()\nSee also: k_fifo_put()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_timeout__test_timeout_non_empty_fifo"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_timeout__test_timeout_non_empty_fifo",
      "summary": "Verify k_fifo_get() returns queued data without waiting."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-timeout-1cpu--test-timeout-empty-fifo",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "On an empty FIFO, k_fifo_get() with a finite timeout must block for at least the requested duration and then return NULL, while K_NO_WAIT must return NULL immediately. The elapsed time is measured to confirm the full timeout elapsed.\nTest steps:\n- Call k_fifo_get() on an empty FIFO with a 10 ms timeout; measure the wait.\n- Verify it returned NULL and that at least the timeout elapsed.\n- Call k_fifo_get() with K_NO_WAIT and verify it returns NULL.\nExpected result:\n- The timed get returns NULL after the timeout; K_NO_WAIT returns NULL at once.\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_empty_fifo"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_empty_fifo",
      "summary": "Verify k_fifo_get() timeout behavior on an empty FIFO."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-timeout-1cpu--test-timeout-fifo-thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A getter pending with a timeout must be woken as soon as a producer thread puts data, returning that data rather than timing out. The test also covers the K_NO_WAIT and K_FOREVER variants where a child thread conditionally supplies data based on availability on a second FIFO, exercising the interaction between blocking gets and producer timing.\nTest steps:\n- Pend on k_fifo_get() with a timeout while a child puts data in time; verify the data is returned within the timeout window.\n- With K_NO_WAIT, verify the child reports no data when the FIFO is empty and reports data when it has been pre-filled.\n- With K_FOREVER, verify the child retrieves pre-filled data.\nExpected result:\n- The getter receives data supplied in time; the reply flags reflect FIFO availability for each timeout variant.\nSee also: k_fifo_get()\nSee also: k_fifo_put()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_fifo_thread"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_fifo_thread",
      "summary": "Verify k_fifo_get() wakes when a thread supplies data within timeout."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-timeout-1cpu--test-timeout-threads-pend-fail-on-fifo",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Several threads pend on the same FIFO with different timeouts; all but the last receive data in time (their timeouts are aborted), and the last one times out. This checks that removing satisfied waiters from the timeout queue leaves the remaining timeout computed correctly, so the final thread still times out as expected.\nTest steps:\n- Spawn threads pending on one FIFO with distinct timeouts.\n- Feed data so all but the last get it in queue order; the last gets none.\n- Verify each satisfied thread reports in order and the last times out.\nExpected result:\n- Satisfied threads report in queue order; the last thread times out cleanly.\nSee also: k_fifo_get()\nSee also: k_fifo_put()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_threads_pend_fail_on_fifo"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_threads_pend_fail_on_fifo",
      "summary": "Verify timeout is recomputed when pending getters are satisfied early."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-timeout-1cpu--test-timeout-threads-pend-on-dual-fifos",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Extends the single-FIFO ordering check to threads distributed across two FIFOs: timeouts must still fire in ascending-timeout order across the combined set, confirming the kernel timeout queue is global and not per-FIFO.\nTest steps:\n- Spawn threads that pend on two different FIFOs with distinct timeouts.\n- Each reports back as it times out; collect the combined order.\nExpected result:\n- Threads time out in increasing-timeout order across both FIFOs.\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_threads_pend_on_dual_fifos"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_threads_pend_on_dual_fifos",
      "summary": "Verify threads pending on two FIFOs time out in global timeout order."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-timeout-1cpu--test-timeout-threads-pend-on-fifo",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "When several threads block on the same FIFO with different timeouts and no data arrives, each must time out in ascending-timeout order regardless of the order in which the threads were queued. This validates the timeout queue ordering for a single FIFO.\nTest steps:\n- Spawn several threads that pend on the same FIFO with distinct timeouts.\n- Each reports back as it times out; collect the order.\nExpected result:\n- Threads time out strictly in increasing-timeout order (within one tick).\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_threads_pend_on_fifo"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_timeout_1cpu__test_timeout_threads_pend_on_fifo",
      "summary": "Verify multiple threads pending on one FIFO time out in timeout order."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-usage--test-dual-fifo-play",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Two FIFOs are used as a request/response channel: the main thread puts to fifo2 and blocks getting from fifo1, while the child blocks getting from fifo2 and puts to fifo1. Control alternates between the threads each iteration, confirming blocking gets correctly serialize the exchange.\nTest steps:\n- Start the child, which loops getting from fifo2 and putting to fifo1.\n- Main thread loops putting to fifo2 and getting from fifo1.\n- Verify each item received on fifo1 matches the expected sequence.\nExpected result:\n- The threads alternate correctly and every item is received in order.\nSee also: k_fifo_put()\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_usage__test_dual_fifo_play"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_usage__test_dual_fifo_play",
      "summary": "Verify ping-pong synchronization across two FIFOs."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-usage--test-isr-fifo-play",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Repeats the two-FIFO hand-off pattern but performs every k_fifo_put() and k_fifo_get() from interrupt context via irq_offload(), confirming the FIFO operations are ISR-safe end to end when both producer and consumer run in an ISR.\nTest steps:\n- Main thread (from an ISR) puts items into fifo2, then starts the child.\n- Child (from ISRs) gets from fifo2 and puts into fifo1, then signals.\n- Main thread (from an ISR) gets the items from fifo1.\nExpected result:\n- All ISR-context put/get operations succeed and items pass in order.\nSee also: k_fifo_put()\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_usage__test_isr_fifo_play"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_usage__test_isr_fifo_play",
      "summary": "Verify producer/consumer exchange with all puts/gets in ISR context."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/fifo-usage--test-single-fifo-play",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Exercises a hand-off pattern on one FIFO: the main thread fills it, a child thread drains it and refills it with a second data set, and the main thread drains that. Confirms items survive a full round trip through both threads in the correct order.\nTest steps:\n- Main thread puts the first data set, then starts the child.\n- Child gets all items, puts the second data set, signals via a semaphore.\n- Main thread gets all items and verifies they match the second data set.\nExpected result:\n- The main thread reads back exactly the items the child enqueued, in order.\nSee also: k_fifo_put()\nSee also: k_fifo_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "fifo_usage__test_single_fifo_play"
        }
      ],
      "name": "fifo_usage__test_single_fifo_play",
      "summary": "Verify producer/consumer exchange over a single FIFO."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
