      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Initialize a memory slab over a caller-provided buffer and verify the defining properties of a memory slab object: every allocated block is a fixed-size region that lies within the provided memory range, the blocks are distinct, the slab provides exactly the configured number of blocks, and a further allocation fails once they are exhausted.\nSee also: k_mem_slab_init(), k_mem_slab_alloc(), k_mem_slab_free()",
