      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The per-CPU structures and the global kernel structure are registered with the object core framework at boot. Using the existing object cores (no new ones are created), confirm each CPU object and the kernel object can be found by walking their respective object types.\nTest steps:\n- Find the CPU object type and walk it for each CPU's object core.\n- Find the kernel object type and walk it for the kernel object core.\nExpected result:\n- Every CPU object core and the kernel object core are found.\nSee also: k_obj_type_find(), k_obj_type_walk_locked(), k_obj_type_walk_unlocked()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core__test_obj_core_system"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core__test_obj_core_system",
      "summary": "Verify per-CPU and kernel objects are registered with the object core framework."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core--test-obj-core-thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Thread objects are registered with the object core framework when created. This test confirms a registered thread can be located through its object type, and that aborting the thread unregisters it from the framework.\nTest steps:\n- Locate the thread object type with k_obj_type_find().\n- Walk the type with k_obj_type_walk_locked()/_unlocked() and confirm both the statically and dynamically created threads are found.\n- Abort both threads.\n- Walk the type again and confirm neither thread is found.\nExpected result:\n- Both threads are found while alive and absent after being aborted.\nSee also: k_obj_type_find(), k_obj_type_walk_locked(), k_obj_type_walk_unlocked()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core__test_obj_core_thread"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core__test_obj_core_thread",
      "summary": "Verify thread objects are tracked and untracked by the object core framework."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core--test-obj-core-timer",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Both a statically defined and a dynamically initialized timer are registered with the object core framework. Confirm the timer object type can be found and that walking it locates both objects.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a timer dynamically with k_timer_init().\n- Find the timer object type and walk it (locked and unlocked) for both the static and dynamic timers.\nExpected result:\n- Both the static and dynamic timer object cores are found.\nSee also: k_obj_type_find(), k_obj_type_walk_locked(), k_obj_type_walk_unlocked()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core__test_obj_core_timer"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core__test_obj_core_timer",
      "summary": "Verify timer objects are registered with the object core framework."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-api--test-obj-core-stats-dereg",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Deregistering statistics removes an object core's backing statistics buffer so that subsequent raw queries fail. This test confirms deregistration is rejected for an object that has no statistics (a semaphore), succeeds for a thread object core, and that raw queries then fail until statistics are re-registered.\nTest steps:\n- Call k_obj_core_stats_deregister() for a semaphore object core.\n- Deregister statistics for the thread object core.\n- Attempt a raw query for the deregistered thread object core.\n- Re-register the thread's statistics buffer.\nExpected result:\n- Deregistration returns -ENOTSUP for the semaphore and 0 for the thread, and the raw query for the deregistered thread returns -EINVAL.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_deregister(), k_obj_core_stats_register()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_dereg"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_dereg",
      "summary": "Verify deregistering statistics detaches the backing buffer from an object core."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-api--test-obj-core-stats-disable",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Statistics can only be disabled for object cores whose type provides a disable operation. This test confirms the API returns -ENOTSUP both for an object type that never supports statistics (a semaphore) and for a thread object core whose disable operation has been temporarily removed.\nTest steps:\n- Call k_obj_core_stats_disable() for a semaphore object core.\n- Clear the thread type's disable operation and call k_obj_core_stats_disable() for the thread object core, then restore it.\nExpected result:\n- Both calls return -ENOTSUP.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_disable()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_disable"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_disable",
      "summary": "Verify k_obj_core_stats_disable() rejects objects without a disable operation."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-api--test-obj-core-stats-enable",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Statistics can only be enabled for object cores whose type provides an enable operation. This test confirms the API returns -ENOTSUP both for an object type that never supports statistics (a semaphore) and for a thread object core whose enable operation has been temporarily removed.\nTest steps:\n- Call k_obj_core_stats_enable() for a semaphore object core.\n- Clear the thread type's enable operation and call k_obj_core_stats_enable() for the thread object core, then restore the operation.\nExpected result:\n- Both calls return -ENOTSUP.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_enable()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_enable"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_enable",
      "summary": "Verify k_obj_core_stats_enable() rejects objects without an enable operation."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-api--test-obj-core-stats-query",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Statistics can only be queried for object cores whose type provides a query operation. This test confirms the API returns -ENOTSUP both for an object type that never supports statistics (a semaphore) and for a thread object core whose query operation has been temporarily removed.\nTest steps:\n- Call k_obj_core_stats_query() for a semaphore object core.\n- Clear the thread type's query operation and call k_obj_core_stats_query() for the thread object core, then restore it.\nExpected result:\n- Both calls return -ENOTSUP.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_query()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_query"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_query",
      "summary": "Verify k_obj_core_stats_query() rejects objects without a query operation."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-api--test-obj-core-stats-raw",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Raw statistics are only available for object cores that provide a raw operation, a valid buffer length and a backing statistics buffer. This test confirms the API reports -ENOTSUP when raw statistics are unsupported and -EINVAL when the buffer length is wrong or the statistics pointer is NULL.\nTest steps:\n- Call k_obj_core_stats_raw() for a semaphore object core.\n- Clear the thread type's raw operation and call it for the thread object core, then restore the operation.\n- Call it for the thread object core with a zero-length buffer.\n- Clear the thread object core's statistics pointer, call it, then restore.\nExpected result:\n- The unsupported cases return -ENOTSUP and the invalid-argument cases return -EINVAL.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_raw()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_raw"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_raw",
      "summary": "Verify k_obj_core_stats_raw() rejects unsupported and invalid raw statistics requests."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-api--test-obj-core-stats-register",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Registering statistics attaches a caller-supplied buffer as an object core's backing statistics storage. This test confirms registration is rejected for an object with no statistics (a semaphore) and when the buffer size is wrong, and that a valid registration redirects raw queries to the new buffer.\nTest steps:\n- Attempt to register statistics for a semaphore object core.\n- Attempt to register a wrong-sized buffer for the thread object core.\n- Register a correctly sized buffer and confirm a raw query reads from it.\n- Restore the thread's original statistics buffer.\nExpected result:\n- Registration returns -ENOTSUP for the semaphore, -EINVAL for the wrong size, and 0 for the valid buffer, after which the raw query reflects that buffer.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_register(), k_obj_core_stats_raw()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_register"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_register",
      "summary": "Verify registering statistics validates its arguments and attaches the backing buffer."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-api--test-obj-core-stats-reset",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Statistics can only be reset for object cores whose type provides a reset operation. This test confirms the API returns -ENOTSUP both for an object type that never supports statistics (a semaphore) and for a thread object core whose reset operation has been temporarily removed.\nTest steps:\n- Call k_obj_core_stats_reset() for a semaphore object core.\n- Clear the thread type's reset operation and call k_obj_core_stats_reset() for the thread object core, then restore it.\nExpected result:\n- Both calls return -ENOTSUP.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_reset()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_reset"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_api__test_obj_core_stats_reset",
      "summary": "Verify k_obj_core_stats_reset() rejects objects without a reset operation."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-mem-block--test-obj-core-stats-mem-block",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "System memory block object cores report raw and queried statistics that track allocations. This test exercises the statistics interface across a sequence of allocations and frees, checking the reported free/allocated bytes and used block counts after each operation, and that resetting the statistics rebases the maximum-usage counters to the current usage.\nTest steps:\n- Sample initial raw and queried stats.\n- Allocate two blocks, freeing one, re-sampling after each step.\n- Reset the stats with k_obj_core_stats_reset() and re-sample.\nExpected result:\n- Every sample matches the expected values and reset rebases the max-usage counters to the current usage.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_raw(), k_obj_core_stats_query(), k_obj_core_stats_reset()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_mem_block__test_obj_core_stats_mem_block"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_mem_block__test_obj_core_stats_mem_block",
      "summary": "Verify querying and resetting statistics for a memory block object core."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-mem-block--test-sys-mem-block-disable",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "System memory block object cores collect statistics unconditionally and do not implement a disable operation. Confirm the disable request is rejected.\nTest steps:\n- Call k_obj_core_stats_disable() for the memory block object core.\nExpected result:\n- The call returns -ENOTSUP.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_disable()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_mem_block__test_sys_mem_block_disable"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_mem_block__test_sys_mem_block_disable",
      "summary": "Verify disabling statistics is unsupported for memory block object cores."
    },
