      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The kernel and per-CPU object cores expose run-time statistics. This test obtains both the raw and queried statistics for these object cores and checks the expected aggregation relationships hold (per-CPU sampling is at least as large as kernel sampling, and the sum across CPUs is at least the kernel total).\nTest steps:\n- Optionally spin up a busy thread per extra CPU to generate activity.\n- Fetch raw stats for the kernel and each CPU with k_obj_core_stats_raw().\n- Fetch queried stats for the kernel and each CPU with k_obj_core_stats_query() and sum the per-CPU values.\nExpected result:\n- Each call returns 0 and the per-CPU/aggregate values are no smaller than the corresponding kernel values.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_raw(), k_obj_core_stats_query()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_system__test_obj_core_stats_system"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_system__test_obj_core_stats_system",
      "summary": "Verify run-time statistics can be queried for the kernel and CPU object cores."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-thread--test-obj-core-stats-thread-test",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Thread object cores expose query, raw, reset, enable and disable statistics operations backed by the thread run-time stats. This test drives a helper thread through known busy/blocked phases and validates the statistics interface end to end:\n- while the thread is blocked its stats do not change;\n- while it runs its execution/total cycles increase;\n- the object core query matches k_thread_runtime_stats_get();\n- resetting clears the counters;\n- disabling freezes the counters and re-enabling resumes collection.\nTest steps:\n- Sample raw and queried stats while the helper thread is blocked, busy-wait, and confirm the samples are unchanged.\n- Let the thread run, re-sample, and confirm cycles increased and the object core query equals k_thread_runtime_stats_get().\n- Reset the stats and confirm the counters are zero.\n- Disable the stats, let the thread run, and confirm the counters are frozen.\n- Re-enable the stats, let the thread run, and confirm the counters advance.\nExpected result:\n- Every operation returns 0 and the sampled statistics behave as described.\nSee also: k_obj_core_stats_raw(), k_obj_core_stats_query(), k_obj_core_stats_reset(), k_obj_core_stats_enable(), k_obj_core_stats_disable()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_thread__test_obj_core_stats_thread_test"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_thread__test_obj_core_stats_thread_test",
      "summary": "Verify the full statistics life cycle for a thread object core."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/object-validation--test-generic-object",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "- The kernel must be able to associate kernel object memory addresses with whether the calling thread has access to that object, the object is of the expected type, and the object is of the expected init state.\n- Test support freeing kernel objects allocated at runtime manually.\nSee also: k_object_alloc(), k_object_access_grant()",
