    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/starve-fn--test-timer-starve",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Repeatedly start and stop timers in a tight, spinlock-protected loop for a sustained period and confirm that the system uptime and tick count keep advancing monotonically without regressing or overflowing.\nSee also: k_uptime_get_32(), sys_clock_tick_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "starve_fn__test_timer_starve"
        }
      ],
      "name": "starve_fn__test_timer_starve",
      "summary": "Verify the uptime clock advances monotonically under timer starvation."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/suite-deadline--test-deadline",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "At equal priority the scheduler must order runnable threads by their deadline (set via k_thread_deadline_set()), running the earliest deadline first. Several equal-priority threads are given random deadlines and must execute in ascending-deadline order.\nTest steps:\n- Create NUM_THREADS equal-priority threads, each recording its run order.\n- Assign each a random deadline, then sleep to let them run.\n- Verify their execution order matches ascending deadline order.\nExpected result:\n- Threads execute earliest-deadline-first.\nSee also: k_thread_deadline_set()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "suite_deadline__test_deadline"
        }
      ],
      "name": "suite_deadline__test_deadline",
      "summary": "Verify EDF threads run in earliest-deadline-first order."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/suite-deadline--test-thread-reschedule",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Changing a thread's deadline does not by itself trigger a context switch; an explicit k_reschedule() must re-evaluate the ready queue and switch to the now earliest-deadline thread. The test orchestrates two EDF helpers and checks the expected thread is selected only after k_reschedule() (exercised via a direct call and, on non-SMP, via irq_offload). Built for single-CPU configs only.\nTest steps:\n- Create two EDF helper threads with different deadlines.\n- Confirm changing a deadline alone causes no switch.\n- Invoke k_reschedule() and confirm the expected thread is then selected.\nExpected result:\n- The scheduler switches to the earliest-deadline thread only on reschedule.\nSee also: k_reschedule()\nSee also: k_thread_deadline_set()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "suite_deadline__test_thread_reschedule"
        }
      ],
      "name": "suite_deadline__test_thread_reschedule",
      "summary": "Verify a deadline change takes effect only on k_reschedule()."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/suite-deadline--test-unqueued",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Setting a deadline on a thread that is still in its start delay (unqueued) must not make it run before its delay elapses. Threads are created with a start delay, given deadlines while unqueued, and must stay dormant until the delay passes.\nTest steps:\n- Create NUM_THREADS threads with a start delay (unqueued).\n- Set a random deadline on each and sleep less than the delay; none must run.\n- Sleep past the delay and confirm all threads then run.\nExpected result:\n- Deadline-set does not start an unqueued thread early; threads run only after their start delay.\nSee also: k_thread_deadline_set()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "suite_deadline__test_unqueued"
        }
      ],
      "name": "suite_deadline__test_unqueued",
      "summary": "Verify k_thread_deadline_set() does not wake a not-yet-started thread."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/suite-deadline--test-yield",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Threads at the same priority and deadline (0) must each get to run when they cooperatively yield. Each worker increments a counter and yields; all must have run by the time the test wakes.\nTest steps:\n- Create NUM_THREADS equal-priority/deadline threads that bump a counter and k_yield().\n- Sleep and verify all threads ran.\nExpected result:\n- Every thread runs, confirming yield rotates among equal peers.\nSee also: k_yield()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "suite_deadline__test_yield"
        }
      ],
      "name": "suite_deadline__test_yield",
      "summary": "Verify k_yield() rotates among equal deadline/priority threads."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/suite-preempt--test-preempt",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Exhaustively checks which thread runs next when a thread is woken, across all priority classes (cooperative, preemptible, meta-IRQ). Threads in each class sleep; a low-priority manager wakes one, which wakes another, and the test validates the next-to-run thread matches the documented preemption rules. The check is repeated for all four combinations of holding/not holding the scheduler lock and for synchronous versus interrupt-context (offloaded) wakes. Single-CPU only.\nTest steps:\n- Create paired threads at cooperative, preemptible and meta-IRQ priorities, all sleeping, plus a manager thread.\n- For each scenario, wake a thread that arranges to wake a target thread.\n- Validate the actually-scheduled thread against the expected one.\nExpected result:\n- The next thread to run always matches the documented preemption rules for every class/lock/context combination.\nSee also: k_wakeup()\nSee also: k_sched_lock()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "suite_preempt__test_preempt"
        }
      ],
      "name": "suite_preempt__test_preempt",
      "summary": "Verify wakeups preempt the running thread per the documented rules."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/suite-preempt-metairq--test-preempt-metairq",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A meta-IRQ thread may preempt a running cooperative thread, but on completion the scheduler must resume that same cooperative thread rather than switching to another ready cooperative thread. The meta-IRQ unblocks a long-running low-priority coop thread, then unblocks a higher-priority coop thread before the first finishes; execution must continue in the low-priority thread and run the high-priority one only afterwards.\nTest steps:\n- Start a meta-IRQ thread and two cooperative threads (low and high priority).\n- The meta-IRQ unblocks the low-priority coop thread, sleeps, then unblocks the high-priority coop thread mid-run.\n- Observe the order in which the coop threads complete.\nExpected result:\n- The preempted low-priority coop thread resumes first; the high-priority coop thread runs after it, confirming the meta-IRQ returns to its preemptee.",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "suite_preempt_metairq__test_preempt_metairq"
        }
      ],
      "name": "suite_preempt_metairq__test_preempt_metairq",
      "summary": "Verify a meta-IRQ returns to the cooperative thread it preempted."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem--test-basic-sem-test",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "sys_sem_init() must validate its arguments and refuse to initialize a semaphore when they are nonsensical, returning -EINVAL rather than producing an unusable object. A valid initialization must then succeed and support a take/give cycle. This case is userspace-only.\nTest steps:\n- Call sys_sem_init() with a NULL semaphore pointer.\n- Call sys_sem_init() with an initial count equal to the max (limit == 0).\n- Call sys_sem_init() with an initial count above the representable range.\n- Call sys_sem_init() with a limit above the representable range.\n- Finally initialize with valid values and perform a take then a give.\nExpected result:\n- Every invalid call returns -EINVAL.\n- The valid initialization succeeds and the take/give cycle completes.\nSee also: sys_sem_init()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem__test_basic_sem_test"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem__test_basic_sem_test",
      "summary": "Verify sys_sem_init() rejects invalid arguments with -EINVAL."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem--test-sem-give-limit",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The count must saturate at the configured maximum: gives up to the limit succeed, and a give at the limit must report -EAGAIN without exceeding the maximum.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 0 and max SEM_MAX_VAL.\n- Give SEM_MAX_VAL times, checking the count rises 1..MAX.\n- Give once more at the limit and inspect the return value and count.\nExpected result:\n- Gives within the limit return 0; a give at the limit returns -EAGAIN and the count never exceeds SEM_MAX_VAL.\nSee also: sys_sem_give()\nSee also: sys_sem_count_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem__test_sem_give_limit"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem__test_sem_give_limit",
      "summary": "Verify sys_sem_give() does not raise the count past its maximum."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem--test-sem-give-take-from-isr-syssem",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Repeated gives from interrupt context must raise the count to the maximum, and repeated takes from interrupt context must lower it back to zero, with the count accurate at every step.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 0.\n- Give from an ISR SEM_MAX_VAL times, checking the count rises 1..MAX.\n- Take from an ISR SEM_MAX_VAL times, checking the count falls MAX-1..0.\nExpected result:\n- The count matches the expected value after every give and take.\nSee also: sys_sem_give()\nSee also: sys_sem_take()\nSee also: sys_sem_count_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem__test_sem_give_take_from_isr_syssem"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem__test_sem_give_take_from_isr_syssem",
      "summary": "Verify give/take from an ISR track the count up and back down."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem--test-sem-take-no-wait-fails-syssem",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "With no tokens available, a non-blocking take must fail with -ETIMEDOUT and must not corrupt or change the count.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 0.\n- Attempt a K_NO_WAIT take five times.\n- After each attempt, read the count.\nExpected result:\n- Every take returns -ETIMEDOUT and the count stays 0.\nSee also: sys_sem_take()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem__test_sem_take_no_wait_fails_syssem"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem__test_sem_take_no_wait_fails_syssem",
      "summary": "Verify sys_sem_take() with K_NO_WAIT fails when count is zero."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem--test-sem-take-no-wait-syssem",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "When tokens are available, sys_sem_take() with K_NO_WAIT must succeed immediately and reduce the count by one each time.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 5.\n- Take with K_NO_WAIT five times.\n- After each take, read the count.\nExpected result:\n- Every take returns 0 and the count decrements 4, 3, 2, 1, 0.\nSee also: sys_sem_take()\nSee also: sys_sem_count_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem__test_sem_take_no_wait_syssem"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem__test_sem_take_no_wait_syssem",
      "summary": "Verify sys_sem_take() succeeds and decrements when count is positive."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem--test-sem-take-timeout-syssem",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A take blocked on a finite timeout must succeed if another thread gives the semaphore before the timeout expires.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 0.\n- Start a thread that gives the semaphore.\n- In the test thread, take with a finite timeout (SEM_TIMEOUT).\nExpected result:\n- The take returns 0 (the give satisfied it before the timeout).\nSee also: sys_sem_take()\nSee also: sys_sem_give()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem__test_sem_take_timeout_syssem"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem__test_sem_take_timeout_syssem",
      "summary": "Verify sys_sem_take() with a timeout succeeds when a give arrives."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem--test-simple-sem-from-isr",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A sys_sem given from interrupt context must increase its available count by one per give, observable via sys_sem_count_get().\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 0.\n- Give the semaphore from an ISR five times.\n- After each give, read the count.\nExpected result:\n- The count equals the number of gives performed so far (1..5).\nSee also: sys_sem_give()\nSee also: sys_sem_count_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem__test_simple_sem_from_isr"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem__test_simple_sem_from_isr",
      "summary": "Verify sys_sem_give() from an ISR increments the count."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem--test-simple-sem-from-task",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The same give-increments-count behavior must hold when invoked from a user-mode thread, exercising the userspace path of the API.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 0.\n- Give the semaphore five times from the (user) test thread.\n- After each give, read the count.\nExpected result:\n- The count equals the number of gives performed so far (1..5).\nSee also: sys_sem_give()\nSee also: sys_sem_count_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem__test_simple_sem_from_task"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem__test_simple_sem_from_task",
      "summary": "Verify sys_sem_give() from a user thread increments the count."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem-1cpu--test-sem-multiple-threads-wait",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "When several threads block taking the same semaphore, one give must release exactly one waiter, so N gives release all N waiters and leave both semaphores drained. Repeated to confirm the behavior is stable across runs.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize the semaphore with count 0.\n- Create TOTAL_THREADS_WAITING helper threads that each block taking the shared semaphore and then give a signalling semaphore.\n- Give the shared semaphore once per helper, then collect one signal per helper and check both semaphore counts.\n- Repeat the whole sequence twice.\nExpected result:\n- Every helper is released (one per give); both counts end at 0 each round.\nSee also: sys_sem_take()\nSee also: sys_sem_give()\nSee also: sys_sem_count_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_multiple_threads_wait"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_multiple_threads_wait",
      "summary": "Verify multiple threads blocked on a sys_sem are each released by a give."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem-1cpu--test-sem-take-kernel-user",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A sys_sem given by a kernel thread must be takeable by a user thread and vice versa, demonstrating that the object works across the privilege boundary.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize two semaphores with count 0.\n- Start a user thread that takes the first semaphore then gives the second.\n- The kernel test thread gives the first semaphore, then takes the second with a finite timeout.\nExpected result:\n- The user thread's take succeeds and the kernel thread's take of the second semaphore returns 0.\nSee also: sys_sem_take()\nSee also: sys_sem_give()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_kernel_user"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_kernel_user",
      "summary": "Verify a sys_sem is shared correctly between kernel and user threads."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem-1cpu--test-sem-take-multiple-syssem",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "When several threads of different priorities are all blocked taking the same semaphore, each give must release the highest-priority waiter first, so the threads complete strictly in priority order.\nTest steps:\n- Create high-, mid-, and low-priority helper threads, each of which takes its own gate semaphore and then blocks taking the shared semaphore.\n- Lower the test thread's priority and release all three gates so the helpers pend on the shared semaphore.\n- Give the shared semaphore once and check which helper progressed; repeat.\nExpected result:\n- The high-priority helper completes on the first give, the mid-priority on the second, and the low-priority on the third \u2014 never out of order.\nSee also: sys_sem_take()\nSee also: sys_sem_give()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_multiple_syssem"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_multiple_syssem",
      "summary": "Verify pended sys_sem takers wake in thread-priority order."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem-1cpu--test-sem-take-timeout-fails-syssem",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "With no token available and no other thread giving, a take with a finite timeout must block for the timeout and then fail with -ETIMEDOUT.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 0.\n- Take with a finite timeout (SEM_TIMEOUT) five times.\nExpected result:\n- Every take returns -ETIMEDOUT after the timeout elapses.\nSee also: sys_sem_take()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_timeout_fails_syssem"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_timeout_fails_syssem",
      "summary": "Verify sys_sem_take() returns -ETIMEDOUT when its timeout expires."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem-1cpu--test-sem-take-timeout-forever-syssem",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A take with K_FOREVER must block indefinitely and wake only when another thread gives the semaphore, then succeed.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 0.\n- Start a thread that sleeps briefly and then gives the semaphore.\n- In the test thread, take with K_FOREVER.\nExpected result:\n- The take returns 0 once the helper thread gives the semaphore.\nSee also: sys_sem_take()\nSee also: sys_sem_give()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_timeout_forever_syssem"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_timeout_forever_syssem",
      "summary": "Verify sys_sem_take() with K_FOREVER blocks until a give arrives."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sys-sem-1cpu--test-sem-take-timeout-isr",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A take blocked on a finite timeout must be woken and succeed when the semaphore is given from interrupt context.\nTest steps:\n- Initialize a semaphore with count 0.\n- Start a thread that gives the semaphore from an ISR.\n- In the test thread, take with a finite timeout (SEM_TIMEOUT).\nExpected result:\n- The take returns 0 (satisfied by the ISR give before the timeout).\nSee also: sys_sem_take()\nSee also: sys_sem_give()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_timeout_isr"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sys_sem_1cpu__test_sem_take_timeout_isr",
      "summary": "Verify a timed sys_sem_take() is satisfied by a give from an ISR."
    },
    {
